**We win on output and speed. We lose on entry cost.** The six concepts a developer must hold before anything runs:

CLI vs standalone vs workspace vs full-app host · workspace root · direct vs bwrap mode · runtime vs app/internal plugin trust · Pi resource vs server `extraTools` · Pi auth-store setup.

> A human should not need to understand the full plugin trust architecture, three app shells, static composition, provisioning, and two skill routers to add one local tool and one skill.

The highest-value work here is **deleting decisions, not adding features**.

## Verified defect — fix first

`packages/plugin-cli/templates/` generates two files that disagree on the panel id:

```
front-canonical.tsx:24   const MAIN_PANEL_ID = "<kebab-name>.page"     ← what gets registered
agent-canonical.ts:12    const PANEL_ID       = "<kebab-name>.panel"   ← what the slash command opens
```

A fresh scaffold registers `.page`; the generated slash command opens `.panel`. It fails only in a live UI, on the developer's **first** interaction with the product. Fix both to one canonical id and add a golden test that fails on drift.

