/home/ubuntu/projects/spike-dx/eve/package/docs/schedules.mdx:96:`:scheduleId` is the path-derived schedule name (`agent/schedules/heartbeat.ts` → `heartbeat`; URL-encode the `/` in nested names). It runs the exact dispatch path the production cron handler uses and returns the started session ids as JSON, so you can subscribe to each one's [stream](./concepts/sessions-runs-and-streaming) at `GET /eve/v1/session/:sessionId/stream`. An unknown id comes back `404` with `availableScheduleIds`, listing the schedules the app actually defines.
