/home/ubuntu/projects/spike-dx/eve/package/docs/tools/human-in-the-loop.md:84:`session` in `approval` has the same shape as `ctx.session` in `execute`: `id`, `auth`, `turn`, and an optional `parent`. If a person later resumes a schedule-started session, `session.auth.current` becomes that person while `session.auth.initiator` remains the app principal. Inspect `initiator` only when the policy should apply to the whole session. Skipping approval on scheduled turns means any non-idempotent side effect will re-fire if a step replays, so pair this pattern with idempotency keys or `once()` where needed.
